{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>He shall be put to death, for he has spoken rebellion against YHWH.</b> Even though he spoke in the name of YHWH and not in the name of idolatry — from which it would appear that he is not liable to the death penalty, as the elders ruled regarding Jeremiah, saying: אֵין לָאִישׁ הַזֶּה מִשְׁפַּט מָוֶת כִּי בְשֵׁם ה׳ אֱלֹהֵינוּ דִּבֶּר אֵלֵינוּ (Jeremiah 26:16) — nevertheless this one is liable to the death penalty because he spoke rebellion in His name." "<b>To seduce you from the way.</b> Even though he did not say 'to seduce you from upon YHWH' — he says in the name of YHWH that you should serve idolatry by His command — he nonetheless seeks to seduce you from the way that YHWH your Elohim has commanded you."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:21:22.273648652Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}